# Architecture

Follow `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

- Layer A is the engine: entities, movement, reservations, commands, objects, world coordinates, serialization, UI extension points.
- Layer B is `src/Modding`: manifests, discovery, dependencies, and later events and commands. It must not depend on gameplay mods.
- Layer C is data and scripts under `mods/`. Do not compile a gameplay mod into `OpenLoco.exe`.
- Prefer a general engine service over a shunting-only or timetable-only structure.
- `src/Modding` is not called from the game loop yet. Do not wire it in until the call site is specified and tested.
- The manifest parser accepts a JSON subset only. Do not treat that parser as a general JSON library.
